# Build-time config for the Vercel production build.
#
# DO NOT move these keys into a plain `.env`. It was tried (PR #8) and it
# took the whole comment layer off the deployed site: Vite reads `.env` in
# every mode locally, so a local build looked identical — same bundle hash —
# while Vercel's build produced a bundle with no API base, no share token,
# and the comment module tree-shaken out entirely, because
# `commentsConfigured` was false. `.env.production` is read; `.env` is not.
# `.env.development` carries the same values for `npm run dev`.
#
# Committed on purpose. Vite inlines `VITE_*` at build time, and the Vercel
# project hosting this site belongs to another account — contributors here
# have repo write but no access to the Vercel dashboard, so committing the
# values is the only route that doesn't depend on someone else.
#
# WHAT IS AND ISN'T SECRET
#
# None of the values below is a secret. The share token is half a credential
# and ships in the client bundle regardless — anyone can read it out of the
# deployed JS. The *passcode* is the actual gate, and it is never in this
# file, in the bundle, or in the repo. The OAuth client id belongs to a
# **public** client: no secret exists for it, and PKCE is what proves a code
# exchange belongs to the browser that started the flow.
#
# That split holds only while the passcode is strong. If it leaks, rotate it:
# BB PM → project → Share links → Manage → key icon → Generate → Save.
# Rotating does NOT change the token, so nothing here needs editing.
#
# TO TURN COMMENTS OFF
#
# Blank `VITE_BBPM_SHARE_TOKEN`. The whole comment layer compiles out and the
# site behaves exactly as it did before it existed — see `commentsConfigured`
# in `src/comments/client.ts`.
#
# TEAM SIGN-IN
#
# `VITE_BBPM_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID` adds "Continue with BB PM" beside the passcode.
# The id below is registered for exactly two redirect URIs, and the
# authorization server refuses every other one:
#
#   https://saramin-eta.vercel.app/oauth/callback   this deployment
#   http://localhost:5173/oauth/callback            npm run dev
#
# A Vercel *preview* deployment gets a one-off origin, so previews fall back
# to the passcode. A new domain needs its own registration — see README →
# Comments. Blank this and the dialog offers the passcode alone.
#
# NEVER put a `bbpm_...` API key in here. That one is a full-account
# credential and would be readable by anyone who opens the page.

VITE_BBPM_API_BASE=https://pm.burningbros.kr/api
VITE_BBPM_SHARE_TOKEN=16574965e46951bb100306f6cc73fd52
VITE_BBPM_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=bbpm_client_c6bed652395b0b7fe35a97023e0c097a
